@* How it works for a buyer (F128.1, Louis's pick 7A): the three steps from a call to a live agent, then the facts a
   business trusts it on. *@
<Band Id="for-you" Kicker="How it works for you">
    <h2 class="chrome reveal">Three steps, and you're live.</h2>
    <ol class="buyer-steps">
        <li><strong>A short call.</strong> We pin down the one job your agent does first, in your words.</li>
        <li><strong>See it work.</strong> A working agent on made-up data, so you see it before anything goes live.</li>
        <li><strong>It's yours.</strong> Your website and its agent, hosted and kept running. Change what it knows by changing a file.</li>
    </ol>
    <TileRow>
        <Tile Title="Your data stays here" Accent="TileAccent.Blue">Hosted in Azure's South African region, in a closed container that sees only what you hand it.</Tile>
        <Tile Title="Every answer measured" Accent="TileAccent.Green" Delay="1">You see what each conversation cost, in rand. No surprises on the bill.</Tile>
        <Tile Title="It sticks to the facts" Accent="TileAccent.Red" Delay="2">It answers from what you give it, and says so when it doesn't know rather than guessing.</Tile>
    </TileRow>
    <p class="band-note"><a href="/pricing">Two plans, from R500 a month</a>.</p>
</Band>
